ADDENDUM: By the way empty cartridge cases ^= ammunition.

Empty cartridge cases really are nothing more than scrap brass; they 
can't explode, or be used in a firearm without being reloaded with 
new powder/primer/projectile, and really shouldn't pose any hazard 
to anyone (unless you forget to wash any lead residue from your hands 
after handling spent brass prior to eating, drinking, smoking, etc.).

