the floor, or I guess you *could* manage to cut yourself on the lip
of a casing if you *really* made an effort, or I suppose you *could*
choke to death if you intentionally stuffed them up your sinuses, 
but excluding those improbable circumstances, I don't think that spent
brass represents an acute public safety hazard sufficient to warrant
prior restraint (unless you routinely supress all scrap metal 
buy/sell/swap ads).
